					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-4255061#post-3629950</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-4255061/scp-8003-j#post-3629950</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 10 Nov 2017 21:42:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrSevere</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>511038</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like the ideas here but not the presentation. You've got two different angles: one is a nihilist who's given up all hope of finding meaning, the other is a lazy employee just trying to get out of work. Realistically there's no reason he can't be both, but narratively it just feels confusing and weird. If it had just been the former it would be an easy upvote, but the weird diversion just didn't work for me.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
